  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 2605.04 Denial of a Local Permit to Sell Display or Consumer Fireworks by Municipality",
  "priorExpiration": "2000-03-31",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2605.04 Denial of a Local Permit to Sell Display or Consumer Fireworks by Municipality.\n\n(a) The municipality shall deny a permit pursuant to RSA 160-B:6, I, if:\n\n(1) The applicant does not have a valid permit for the sale of fireworks, pursuant to title 18 of the United States Code;\n\n(2) The applicant does not have a place of business within the municipality;\n\n(3) The business will not be located in a permanent structure;\n\n(4) The building in which the business will be located, including any storage facility, does not comply with applicable fire safety codes, building codes, zoning codes and local ordinances, including all applicable provisions of the state building code and the state fire code pursuant to Saf-C 6000;\n\n(5) The applicant has been convicted of a felony which has not been annulled; or\n\n(6) The applicant is younger than 21 years of age.\n\nSource. #5752, eff 12-2-93; ss by INTERIM #7140, eff 12-2-99, EXPIRED: 3-31-00\n\nNew. #7905, eff 6-24-03; ss by #8519, eff 12-16-05; ss by #10784, eff 2-13-15",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2600.html"
